course: dictionary
lesson: 5725
title: A plant with an unknown name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You may never have seen a plant called loosestrife, but the words around it can help. «Purple loosestrife arrived early, shaking luxuriant tangled locks along the edge of the mirror.» The mirror is the still water of the river, and the plant grows along its edge, so loosestrife must be a plant that lives near water.
explain: More clues come from the description. The plant has purple flowers, and it is tall and tangled, like hair blown by a breeze. Loosestrife is a plant with purple or yellow flowers that grows in damp places like rivers and ponds.
explain: Now check your idea by swapping in the meaning. Could you say «Purple water plant arrived early» and still make sense? Yes, so you have understood the word. If you are not sure, a dictionary will confirm it.
fact: Loosestrife is a tall wild plant that grows by rivers, ponds and in damp places.
fact: Purple loosestrife has spikes of bright purple-pink flowers, and yellow loosestrife has yellow flowers.
fact: In «The Wind in the Willows», purple loosestrife is one of the summer flowers on the riverbank.
fact: Loosestrife is a habitat for bees and butterflies, which means it is a place where they live.
fact: In North America, purple loosestrife came from Europe, and it is an invasive weed that crowds out native plants.
exercise: «Purple loosestrife arrived early, shaking luxuriant tangled locks along the edge of the mirror.» Where does the loosestrife grow? | Inside a castle | Inside a dry desert | *Along the edge of the water | On the top of a mountain
exercise: Loosestrife is a what? | A type of rock | A kind of boat | *A tall wild plant | A bird that sings at dawn
exercise: In North America, purple loosestrife is an invasive weed. What does that suggest? | A fish that lives in rivers | A garden rose grown for its scent | *A weed that crowds out other plants | A tree that drops its leaves in winter
test: Purple loosestrife has spikes of bright purple-pink flowers. What colour are they? | Green | *Bright purple-pink | Black | White
test: Which creatures use loosestrife as a habitat? | Sharks and whales | *Bees and butterflies | Owls and foxes | Lions and tigers
exam: Bees and butterflies use loosestrife as a habitat. What does habitat mean here? | *A place where a living thing lives | A kind of flower | A type of bee | A river boat
